# Pipwatch is a static, client-side app — there are no API keys, server
# secrets, or .env files to worry about. Everything it stores (accounts,
# trades, chart screenshots) lives in the browser's localStorage, never in
# this folder, so a plain `git add .` is normally safe. This file exists to
# catch the few ways real trading data could still end up in the repo.

# Backup files exported from the Accounts tab. These contain your full
# trade history (entries, exits, P/L, notes) and any attached chart
# screenshots — never commit one of these to a public (or shared) repo.
pipwatch-backup-*.json
*.backup.json
backups/

# A leftover profile folder from an older version of the launch scripts
# that opened the app in a dedicated browser window. Harmless, but it's
# local browser-profile data, not app source, so it doesn't belong in git.
.pipwatch-app-profile/

# OS-generated junk
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Editor/IDE folders
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Just in case you ever add a build step, a local server, or any script
# that reads credentials from the environment later on:
.env
.env.*
*.local
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
